# User command instructions

When the user needs to run something locally (git pull, build, reload extension, release prep, etc.):

- **Always give the full command block** — every command, in order, ready to copy and paste.
- Use absolute or `~/`-based paths matching their setup: `~/ws/scriptdir/scripts/general/OpenDir/opendir-extension`
- Do not say "run npm run build" without the preceding `cd` and any required `git pull`.
- Do not hand off partial steps or assume they know which directory to be in.
- Include reload/reminder lines after build when relevant (Chrome extension reload).

Example format (include discard before pull — local `npm run build` often modifies `manifest.json`):

```bash
cd ~/ws/scriptdir/scripts/general/OpenDir
git restore opendir-extension/manifest.json
git pull origin cursor/fix-truncated-filenames-cd8c
cd opendir-extension
npm run build
grep '"version"' dist/manifest.json
```

If `git restore` is not enough or you have other local edits to keep, stash instead of discard:

```bash
cd ~/ws/scriptdir/scripts/general/OpenDir
git stash push -m "before opendir pull" -- opendir-extension/manifest.json
git pull origin cursor/fix-truncated-filenames-cd8c
cd opendir-extension
npm run build
grep '"version"' dist/manifest.json
```

Then: reload `opendir-extension/dist/` in Chrome at `chrome://extensions`.
